{"title":"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0073ed91e1a9a1cda445af237b7b67815147c979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JKLM$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" /> is drawn with its vertices on the sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bf1e5a1f898db422b11eb7246758290046d9386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PJ = PK = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"14\" /> m, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/498d2203eeef25f0a4a2a64d57e8462925343e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JQ = KR = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" /> m, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddf714d449b9c6ffe450fdbb57763660b3ee8f29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> m, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1e54de87ff17f00d801c9de48ffd0dc0b15494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR = 66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> m, as shown\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(put graph on problem 2 page)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/e/58ed6bb8ec560c108f71ad7fc44cab584c821d04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ML$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41f7b339156e9d76933e8c0831b2fd1fe3ffe17c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JM$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />, we can use rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0073ed91e1a9a1cda445af237b7b67815147c979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JKLM$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(only rectangle JKLM)\n</p><p>Since opposite sides are equal in a rectangle, we can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffcbdd9ddf4814ea912ab49d3e4ba1cbe434cc5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JM = KL = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"129\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>However, we can notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78dba1db7d15cf8806626e514b9275093521ad3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d622ca8b491b7ad6a2bf6ec11c4480c6091e26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />, the hypotenuses of the right triangles, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41f7b339156e9d76933e8c0831b2fd1fe3ffe17c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JM$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef091d889893c7c10e475a93e4ef626ff70aa5ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, one of the legs are equal. Thus, we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa9fdfc7e3dbf297661872cfcd90d0ae00389837.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MQ = LR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2a\">part a</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7f1156c0f283480848554450ede7d4be2daf2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MQ = LR = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Next, we notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/b/17ba2552921c235a1042cef997dadb9bcfec5509.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR = MQ + ML + LR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"18\" />. Plugging in the values we know, we see:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/5/1556e2a0bfd2ff5ccc73d25d79a08b0726f8f1d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66 = 30 + ML + 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"157\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8edbaf92d1225c6fafdb487645e98318ef24db86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ML + 60 = 66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/911259c0d3bd0596631b6237ca8aa9ea13133de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ML = 66 - 60 = \\boxed{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"161\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/6/746d88459bb1a1a853f0b1bfc2f2e66e52bd8072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = PR = PJ + JQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" /> from the diagram and fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be733cd1c4f79f21c1e0ada0bbb957b51db5432b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = PR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />. Plugging in the values we know, we see:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/e/c6e082b5ce53d43f1a41287d4cfd9dba3871188a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = PR = 50 + 5 = 55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Next, we notice that triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c587b0c1e5de0bde79b9d8c36913c16dee04d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/d/1cd90089f00dba535ce1a385be52da4c29010385.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PJK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> are similar because they share the same angles, which can be shown by setting the measure of the angles that are equal in triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c587b0c1e5de0bde79b9d8c36913c16dee04d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and then we notice that angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/7/2473ec067617b5c5fb346e6340ca42b2636ad9eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JPK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> is shared, so the other angles that are equal to each other in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/d/1cd90089f00dba535ce1a385be52da4c29010385.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PJK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> must also be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daa000ced60b97f75006db987fbd651210ce52f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{PQ}{PJ} = \\frac{QR}{JK}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in values we know, we see:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/2/9f203b82e8c32b51a673e91ee70f3e819a951b99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{55}{5} = \\frac{66}{JK}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82dc6a6ba83b136d283da2e1c01a4ecc537f93a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 = \\frac{66}{JK}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/6/bc6c1541246536c9570bb44304d6a8196d3ce5e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK = \\frac{66}{11} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"110\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Next, we can focus on rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0073ed91e1a9a1cda445af237b7b67815147c979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JKLM$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(rectangle JKLM but showcasing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56e8bc23044402bf5314f8ac1bcd5c1d5311d189.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />)\n</p><p>From the rectangle, we notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba8417c664e9b586a2b5c83f9f9198b399d1bd54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK = ML$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> because they are opposite sides in the rectangle. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad80985a97f4180efda351258f5b123037150349.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ML = \\boxed{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"78\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018012732\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.048 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 180/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2334/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6640/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   18.661      1 -total\n 72.30%   13.491      1 2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n 29.75%    5.551      5 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35554:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018012732 and revision id 277901. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}